This paper investigates the normalized ground state solution for the given biharmonic Choquard type equation \begin{align*}
  \begin{split}
  -\Delta^2u=-\left(\frac{1}{|x|^\mu}*f(x)\right)f(x)\quad\text{in}\ \ \mathbb{R}^4,
  \end{split}
  \end{align*} under specific assumptions about the function $f$, and provides a proof of its existence using a combination of mathematical and topological methods and properties of the fractional $\frac{2}{\mu}$-Riesz potential.
